From the user input, and using the guide below, you will implement a new tRPC
router.

# Hands on guide

Below is a hands on guide on the patterns used in this project to implement a
new tRPC router.

## File Structure

```
server/trpc/
├── index.ts     # Main app router (merges all other routers)
└── [route].ts   # Domain-specific routers (e.g., users.ts, files.ts, items.ts)
```

## Basic Router Template

```typescript
// server/trpc/items.ts
import { and, desc, eq } from "drizzle-orm";
import * as z from "zod";
// import the table from the schema
import { TItems } from "~~/server/db/schema";
// import the router and procedure helpers
import { createTRPCRouter, protectedProcedure } from "../lib/trpc";

export const itemsRouter = createTRPCRouter({
  // LIST: get all items for the current user
  // use protectedProcedure for authenticated routes
  list: protectedProcedure
    // no input needed for list, but you can add pagination:
    // .input(z.object({ limit: z.number().optional().default(10) }))
    .query(async ({ ctx }) => {
      return await ctx.db
        .select()
        .from(TItems)
        // always filter by user id for user-scoped data
        .where(eq(TItems.userId, ctx.session.user.id))
        .orderBy(desc(TItems.createdAt))
        // always use .all() for lists - it throws an error if the query fails
        .all();
    }),

  // CREATE: insert a new item
  create: protectedProcedure
    // always use zod for input validation
    // always add defaults in the schema if possible
    .input(z.object({ name: z.string().min(1).max(255) }))
    .mutation(async ({ input, ctx }) => {
      return await ctx.db
        .insert(TItems)
        // always include userId for user-scoped data
        .values({ name: input.name, userId: ctx.session.user.id })
        .returning()
        // always use .get() for single results - it throws an error if the query
        // fails
        .get();
    }),

  // UPDATE: update an existing item
  update: protectedProcedure
    .input(
      z.object({ id: z.string().uuid(), name: z.string().min(1).max(255) }),
    )
    .mutation(async ({ input, ctx }) => {
      return await ctx.db
        .update(TItems)
        .set({ name: input.name })
        // always check both id AND userId to prevent unauthorized access
        .where(
          and(eq(TItems.id, input.id), eq(TItems.userId, ctx.session.user.id)),
        )
        .returning()
        .get();
    }),

  // DELETE: remove an item
  delete: protectedProcedure
    .input(z.object({ id: z.string().uuid() }))
    .mutation(async ({ input, ctx }) => {
      // delete doesn't need to return anything
      await ctx.db
        .delete(TItems)
        .where(
          and(eq(TItems.id, input.id), eq(TItems.userId, ctx.session.user.id)),
        );
    }),
});
```

## Registering a Router

After creating a router, register it in the main app router:

```typescript
// server/trpc/index.ts
import type { inferRouterInputs, inferRouterOutputs } from "@trpc/server";
import { itemsRouter } from "~~/server/trpc/items";
import { baseProcedure, createTRPCRouter } from "../lib/trpc";

export const appRouter = createTRPCRouter({
  // public health check endpoints
  ping: baseProcedure.query(() => "pong"),
  health: baseProcedure.query(() => ({ status: "ok" })),

  // register domain routers
  items: itemsRouter,
});

// export type definition of API for client usage
export type AppRouter = typeof appRouter;
export type AppRouterInputs = inferRouterInputs<AppRouter>;
export type AppRouterOutputs = inferRouterOutputs<AppRouter>;
```

## Using Context Services

The context (`ctx`) provides access to various services. Check
[`server/lib/trpc.ts`](mdc:server/lib/trpc.ts) for the full context definition.

```typescript
// ctx.db - Drizzle database instance
const items = await ctx.db.select().from(TItems).all()

// ctx.storage - Cloudflare R2 file storage
await ctx.storage.put(key, file)
await ctx.storage.get(key)
await ctx.storage.del(key)
const files = await ctx.storage.list(prefix)
const url = await ctx.storage.presign(key)

// ctx.vector - Cloudflare Vectorize for embeddings
await ctx.vector.set(key, vector, metadata)
await ctx.vector.get(key)
await ctx.vector.del(key)
const results = await ctx.vector.search(vector, topK)

// ctx.queue - Cloudflare Queues for background jobs
await ctx.queue.send({ type: 'process', data: { ... } })

// ctx.session - Better Auth session (available in protectedProcedure)
ctx.session.user.id
ctx.session.user.email
ctx.session.session.id

// ctx.event - H3 event for advanced use cases
ctx.event.headers
ctx.event.waitUntil(asyncTask) // for background tasks
```

## File Upload Handling

For file uploads, use FormData with zod transforms:

```typescript
import { createTRPCRouter, protectedProcedure } from "../lib/trpc";
import { onFileUpload } from "../tasks/onFileUpload";

export const filesRouter = createTRPCRouter({
  create: protectedProcedure
    .input(
      z
        // accept FormData from the client
        .instanceof(FormData)
        // transform to object for easier access
        .transform((fd) => Object.fromEntries(fd.entries()))
        // then validate the shape
        .pipe(
          z.object({
            file: z
              .instanceof(File)
              .refine((f) => f.size > 0, "File is empty")
              .refine(
                (f) => f.size <= 10 * 1024 * 1024,
                "File too large (max 10MB)",
              )
              .refine((f) => ["text/plain", "text/markdown"].includes(f.type)),
          }),
        ),
    )
    .mutation(async ({ input, ctx }) => {
      // namespace files by user id
      const key = `${ctx.session.user.id}/${input.file.name}`;
      await ctx.storage.put(key, input.file);

      // trigger background processing with waitUntil
      ctx.event.waitUntil(onFileUpload(key, ctx));

      return { key };
    }),
});
```

## Procedure Types

- `baseProcedure`: Public procedure with logging. Use for health checks, public
  data.
- `protectedProcedure`: Requires authentication, throws 401 if no session. Use
  for all user-scoped data.
